statement:
The text is generated from the definitions in declaration order: `
/* file generated by qcc, do not modify */

typedef struct
{	int	pad[28];
`, then one line per global definition before `end_sys_globals`, then `} globalvars_t;

`, then `typedef struct
{
`, one line per field definition before `end_sys_fields`, and `} entvars_t;

`. A line is `	<ctype>	<name>;
` with `<ctype>` `float` for float, `vec3_t` for vector, `string_t` for string, `func_t` for function and `int` for every other type; a vector's `_x`, `_y` and `_z` definitions get no line of their own.
